        "screened_from": 18540,
        "prior_work": "NSAIDs inhibit prostaglandin synthesis, essential for gastric mucosal protection. This mechanism and the association between NSAID use and gastrointestinal complications are well-established in pharmacological and epidemiological literature.",
        "why_this_cohort": "COMPASS (Chicago Multiethnic Prevention And Surveillance Study) is a community-based cohort with detailed, multi-module questionnaire data on medication use (including Celebrex), health diagnoses (including reflux), and demographic and behavioral covariates. The cohort structure allows for cross-sectional analysis of reflux prevalence by Celebrex exposure, with retrospective age at diagnosis available."
